From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 15:38:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mips: smp-mt: skip stray Compare arm when mips_hpt_frequency is uncalibrated

vsmp_smp_finish() unconditionally arms CP0 Compare on every secondary CPU
bring-up using mips_hpt_frequency, with no guard for platforms that never
calibrate it -- econet doesn't (a separate external HPT peripheral is the
real clockevent source here; nothing in arch/mips/econet/ ever sets
mips_hpt_frequency). With mips_hpt_frequency=0, the arithmetic silently
degenerates to write_c0_compare(read_c0_count()), arming an immediate/
spurious Compare-elapsed condition on every secondary CPU the moment it
comes online, instead of the intended no-op. Every other user of
mips_hpt_frequency in this tree already guards against exactly this
(cevt-r4k.c, csrc-r4k.c) -- this call site was simply missed. No behavior
change on any platform that does calibrate the frequency.

Found while chasing a reproducible CPU0/CPU1 timer-IRQ rate imbalance on
EN751221; whether that's the same bug is not established, but this call
site is wrong on an uncalibrated platform either way.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
---
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/smp-mt.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/smp-mt.c
@@ -120,8 +120,21 @@ static void vsmp_init_secondary(void)
 
 static void vsmp_smp_finish(void)
 {
-	/* CDFIXME: remove this? */
-	write_c0_compare(read_c0_count() + (8* mips_hpt_frequency/HZ));
+	/*
+	 * CDFIXME: remove this?
+	 * Skip when mips_hpt_frequency is uncalibrated (0): not every MIPS-MT
+	 * platform uses CP0's own Count/Compare pair as its clockevent source
+	 * (e.g. econet: a separate external HPT peripheral is used instead,
+	 * and nothing ever calibrates this variable), and the arithmetic
+	 * below silently degenerates to write_c0_compare(read_c0_count()),
+	 * arming an immediate/spurious Compare-elapsed condition on every
+	 * secondary CPU bring-up instead of doing nothing useful. Matches the
+	 * defensive !mips_hpt_frequency check every other user of this
+	 * variable already has (cevt-r4k.c, csrc-r4k.c) -- a no-op for any
+	 * platform that does calibrate it, so no behavior change there.
+	 */
+	if (mips_hpt_frequency)
+		write_c0_compare(read_c0_count() + (8 * mips_hpt_frequency / HZ));
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_MIPS_MT_FPAFF
 	/* If we have an FPU, enroll ourselves in the FPU-full mask */
